we should be ready for a fight.

257
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:13,690
Dressrosa, huh?

258
00:14:13,773 --> 00:14:16,397
You said you needed to go
there too, right, Keen?

259
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,520
Yes, indeed!

260
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,367
One of my comrades is there!

261
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,080
Held prisoner by our foe!

262
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,920
Please, leave him alone!

263
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:29,377
We've done his mess, man!

264
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:30,290
Stop it!

265
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:33,060
You can't take him from us! Please!

266
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,617
We're nothing but a bunch of misfits!

267
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,397
He's the only one who has faith in us!

268
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,539
We'll be finished!

269
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,020
Oh, don't you worry.

270
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:47,217
Much as I wish I could,
I can't read minds.

271
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:50,757
So every last one of you might
know more than you should not

272
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:55,100
just you same goes for law on the
Straw Hat the whole island, too

273
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,440
So I'll just have to kill you all

274
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,340
Hold on there

275
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,680
Pardon me for the intrusion

276
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:17,140
I'm afraid I need you to step aside

277
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:29,280
That man you intend on killing right there

278
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:31,880
He's an old friend of mine

279
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:37,360
Whoa, what the hell's Aokiji doing here?

280
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:56,480
Oh, no!

281
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:58,380
Young master!

282
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:39,680
I'm not really looking
to pick a fight with you.

283
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:44,151
But you should encourage your
friend to keep his trap shut.

284
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:47,269
You might not like how
things go otherwise.

285
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:52,620
While we're here, let me
ask you something. Hm?

286
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,060
You're not a marine.

287
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:57,440
So what the hell are you, Kuzan?

288
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:07,140
Your reputation's not too good these days.

289
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:13,597
Are you going to give the
man some first aid or what?

290
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,820
Oh, yes, sir!

291
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:31,044
There's a difference in the look of a
vagabond and that of a man newly determined.

292
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,860
He's found a purpose.

293
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:35,400
You can see it in his eyes.

294
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:40,809
I never thought the world
government was absolute, you know.

295
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:43,437
There's plenty of things I can accomplish

296
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:46,277
in this world without
being a navy admiral.

297
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,077
And plenty of things I can see now that I

298
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:53,700
was blind to before I was as good as dead.

299
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:03,297
Well maybe it was faith that brought
me here—why'd you really come here?

300
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:05,237
I came to see you!

301
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:06,150
you

302
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:08,420
And how did you know where I'd be?

303
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:10,440
Ah, damn it.

304
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,897
Don't tell me you're in with
the black market dealers now.

305
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:14,810
Is that it?

306
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,060
How do you go from the Navy to that?

307
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,948
If you're done patching
them up, then scram!

308
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:30,340
Smoker, I'm still me. All right?

309
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:33,080
Then I can trust you.

310
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:36,780
Anyway, you should keep
an eye on Doflamingo.

311
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:40,660
He's not just a warlord,
but the king of Dressrosa.

312
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:44,097
And don't think that makes him
like the snake princess, either.

313
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:47,440
He's in a class of his own,
as dangerous as they come.

314
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:51,140
Tell Sakazuki to mobilize
the admirals right away.

315
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:55,114
Worst case scenario, things
could go wrong very quickly.

316
00:18:56,260 --> 00:19:00,457
This will be the biggest challenge
he's faced as fleet admiral for sure.

317
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:02,620
Maybe the biggest in his life.

318
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:05,440
Well, you've been warned.

319
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:14,057
One last thing—don't
tell anyone you saw me.

320
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:14,970
If

321
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:17,797
word gets out then uh.

322
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:18,710
Who

323
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:22,690
cares?

324
00:19:22,773 --> 00:19:23,603
Never

325
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,937
mind then later.

326
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:26,900
later

327
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:42,737
We've made it to the end of the day.

328
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,480
No enemy sighted anywhere.

329
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:51,400
Sir, no enemy's found on my patrol either.
Good work. At ease, soldier. Thank you.

330
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:57,640
Hey, are we safe yet or what?

331
00:19:57,860 --> 00:19:59,797
How many people are looking for us?

332
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:00,937
Like a whole army?

333
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:02,937
I'm afraid the second I lay down,

334
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:06,079
Doflamingo's gonna swoop
in and kill me in my sleep!

335
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,462
He's gonna get all of us killed!

336
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,485
He gave us these cool helmets!

337
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:12,517
I bet we're, like, invincible now!

338
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,317
Designing from the warlords of the seer,

339
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,577
go into battle with one
of the four emperors.

340
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:20,189
Obviously, he'll pass on both
and come kill us if he's wise.

341
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,040
Oh, I'm scared.

342
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:28,149
Stop fleeing and face your
punishment, you spineless coward!

343
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:35,200
Don't jump to conclusions,
it's complicated. Get away!

344
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,417
Would you stop fighting on the ship?

345
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:39,597
You're gonna sink us all!

346
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:42,457
You guys playing Samurai? Fight! Fight!

347
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:43,599
Have you no shame?

348
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,760
The wanted kingdom heartbroken!

349
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,880
The brave of our hero!

350
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:50,870
Defiled!

351
00:20:50,953 --> 00:20:52,760
I told you I couldn't take it!

352
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:56,237
Am I to believe that our hero
Ryuba's legendary blade, Chouchou,

353
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:57,817
simply fell into your lap?

354
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:59,537
You're a real pal, Samurai.

355
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:01,260
Cut them in half for me.

356
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:04,440
Hey, guys, how's the midnight
snack sound? Awesome!

357
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:06,200
What's on the menu? Pizza.

358
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,010
Pita?

359
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:10,517
I am not familiar with this dish by name,

360
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:13,306
but if your chef made
it, I'm eager to try it.

361
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,477
Did Momonosuke go to bed already?

362
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,337
He's taking a bath with Robin right now.

363
00:21:17,420 --> 00:21:18,250
What?

364
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:26,860
You haven't had a chance to bathe
in days, have you? Quite true.

365
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:30,645
Are you all nice and warm now?

366
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:32,110
Indeed.

367
00:21:32,193 --> 00:21:33,100
Most relaxing.

368
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,280
Oh, perfect timing.

369
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,647
Kin'emon, he needs some
clothes, if you would.

370
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:44,540
What are you grinning about,
you dirty little brat?

371
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:48,760
We can see right through
that act of yours.

372
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:52,337
You think you can get away with
this just because you're a kid?

373
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:55,067
You must now cut off
your top knot and shame.

374
00:21:57,960 --> 00:22:01,700
Hey, why are you ganging
up on a child, you jerks?

375
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:04,220
He's a man in his heart.

376
00:22:04,520 --> 00:22:06,720
Do not let him fool you, Nami.

377
00:22:07,540 --> 00:22:10,340
Say I feel the part of the princess.

378
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,377
You think I'm a princess?

379
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:13,980
Well, I won't disagree.

380
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:17,520
Aw, you're such a good boy.

381
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:20,018
You sleep with me and Robin tonight.

382
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:21,390
No!

383
00:22:21,473 --> 00:22:23,277
Their bedroom is a secret garden.

384
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:24,536
You don't get to go.

385
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:27,730
What?!

386
00:22:27,813 --> 00:22:30,040
You're a filthy little devil, I knew it!

387
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:39,637
I just know Doflamingo's gonna
sneak up on us in the dead of night.

388
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,317
Getting over with already, man?

389
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,457
Better yet, just don't come at all!

390
00:22:43,540 --> 00:22:45,660
We can never fall asleep again!

391
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:52,080
Looks like the horizon is all clear. Yep.

392
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:14,960
It's the news.

393
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:20,780
Look, there's a story about Doflamingo.

394
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,780
It says here.

395
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,110
He resigned!

396
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:28,994
And he gave up the throne of Dressrosa?

397
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:30,260
What is that about?

398
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:34,127
Huh, if he had a throne, then
doesn't that mean he was a king?

399
00:23:34,620 --> 00:23:35,450
Him, really?

400
00:23:35,533 --> 00:23:37,186
Who would that guy rule over?

401
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:38,480
Birds, I guess.

402
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:39,737
Ain't to be a downer,

403
00:23:39,820 --> 00:23:43,397
but don't you think this whole thing's
working out to be a little too convenient?

404
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,833
Nah, it's a good thing.

405
00:23:45,380 --> 00:23:48,439
I mean, since he didn't
have a choice in the matter.

406
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:51,557
Hey, look at that!

407
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:54,169
There's a picture of
me and Traffy in here!

408
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:57,540
Trafalgar Law of the Seven Warlords?

409
00:23:58,120 --> 00:24:00,840
Forms an alliance with
the Straw Hat Pirates?

410
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:05,600
It remains to be seen how the government
will choose to punish Law. Oh dear.

411
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:08,771
Sure is a lot going on in the world today!

412
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:14,694
Dove Lamingo quit the Warlords and
now Law's working with the Straw Hats?

413
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:23,800
And then, to top it all off, Captain
Kidd, Scratchman Apu, Basil Hawkins.

414
00:24:24,140 --> 00:24:26,657
It says the Kidd Pirates,
the Honor Pirates,

415
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:29,517
and the Hawkins Pirates have
formed an alliance though too.

416
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:32,247
Man, today's news just
keeps getting crazier.

417
00:24:32,340 --> 00:24:33,480
I wonder why.

418
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:36,837
Those are the troublemakers we've
been keeping an eye on for two years.

419
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:39,157
So why are they in
cahoots all of a sudden?

420
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:42,537
It looks like things are about
to get intense in the new world.

421
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:43,450
This is huge.

422
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:46,797
I can't believe all those crews have
decided to join forces like that.

423
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,233
Yeah, just like we did.

424
00:24:48,460 --> 00:24:50,872
I guess we had the right idea, didn't we?

425
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:52,459
Forget about them.

426
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,419
Let's stick with our original plan.

427
00:24:56,520 --> 00:24:58,740
We'll keep our focus on Doflamingo.

428
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:04,037
Think about it.

429
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:08,061
Yesterday's negotiation was more
crucial for him than you realized.

430
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:11,654
All we did was kidnap Caesar, remember?

431
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,577
And yet practically overnight,

432
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:17,897
he gave up not only the throne he's
been sitting on for the past 10 years,

433
00:25:17,980 --> 00:25:20,817
but also the government's Carrot
blanche he was given as a privilege.

434
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:22,371
when he became a warlord.

435
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:28,297
If he did that just to get Caesar back,
that should tell us a lot about his motives.

436
00:25:28,380 --> 00:25:30,500
Please answer us, your majesty!

437
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:51,900
It's me—you'll be happy to
know I've resigned. resigned
